      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T20:32:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we just standardize on this name and get rid of finalizeGradientStorage?\n\nI like that CacheStorageData is more general than the gradientStorage name, but it would be good if we can name it something that also indicates that the caching has to happen before data appending. Maybe something like \"finalizePrecachedStorageData\" or \"finalizeRecordTimeStorageData\"?",
