      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 3948337
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-07T15:49:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`finalizeGradientStorage()` should have been private; but this was lost in translation.\n\nMy thinking is that we want both `finalizeGradientStorage` and `finalizePrecachedStorageData`. The idea is that the StorageContext can be extended to maintain multiple caches, each in a self contained struct. So `finalizePrecachedStorageData` would call all the child finalizes.\n\nBut after writing the above, I think multiple caches would require interleaving the data to get valid offsets, so only a single finalize would be required. (As opposed to each cache having their own private data stream which gets concatenated in the buffer `finalize`).",
      "parentUuid": "2b4750d4_8f34651f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 58,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "a214142580858219295364f80560f84fb2e38ce3",
